; Willy's walk frame: step counter and sprite frame
;
; Bits 0-1 only (0-3): the frame of the Willy sprite within the half chosen by the facing bit of
; #R$85D0 (#R$9637 adds frame * 32 to the sprite address), and the step timer of #R$8DD3. While he
; walks, the frame counts 3 down to 0 when facing left and 0 up to 3 when facing right, one count per
; pass, and the cell step is taken in the pass that finds it at 0 (left) or 3 (right): after the
; step it is reloaded with 3 (left) or 0 (right). So a step takes 4 passes and the four frames
; are shown once per step. It keeps its value when he stops, so a new walk resumes in the middle of
; the cycle. In the ending stages 2 and 3 the frame loop sets bit 0 in every pass (#R$89AD, $8A00)
; which speeds the animation up. Saved at room entry in #R$85D7.
@label=WillyFrame
g$85D2 DEFB $00
